  "description": "Wires the cr-sqlite extension into EF Core so several replicas of a SQLite database can be written independently and merged without conflicts — per column, not per row, so two devices editing different fields of the same record both keep their work. Application code stays ordinary EF Core: LINQ, change tracking, SaveChanges. Handles the integration details that otherwise fail quietly — loading the extension on every connection, finalizing before close, giving every column a default so peers on older schemas can still apply changes, and promoting tables to replicated relations after the schema exists. Exposes the change feed as an ordered log, ready to ship to peers.",
